From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jake Hoffman <122403457+jakethehoffer@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 12:02:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] core: do not define a valueless _XOPEN_SOURCE on QNX

flb_coro.h and flb_output.h define _XOPEN_SOURCE with no value when it is not
set (needed on macOS for ucontext). QNX's <sys/platform.h> accepts only the
values 500, 600 and 700 and stops with "#error This version of XOPEN_SOURCE
is not supported" (sys/platform.h, line 172 in SDP 8.0), so every translation
unit that includes either header fails to compile.

QNX needs no such definition, so skip it when __QNXNTO__ is defined.

Signed-off-by: Jake Hoffman <122403457+jakethehoffer@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 include/fluent-bit/flb_coro.h   | 3 ++-
 include/fluent-bit/flb_output.h | 3 ++-
 2 files changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/include/fluent-bit/flb_coro.h b/include/fluent-bit/flb_coro.h
index e069a7c..d34148f 100644
--- a/include/fluent-bit/flb_coro.h
+++ b/include/fluent-bit/flb_coro.h
@@ -21,7 +21,8 @@
 #define FLB_CORO_H
 
 /* Required by OSX */
-#ifndef _XOPEN_SOURCE
+/* QNX rejects a valueless _XOPEN_SOURCE and needs none */
+#if !defined(_XOPEN_SOURCE) && !defined(__QNXNTO__)
 #define _XOPEN_SOURCE
 #endif
 
diff --git a/include/fluent-bit/flb_output.h b/include/fluent-bit/flb_output.h
index 2c7d801..7053e45 100644
--- a/include/fluent-bit/flb_output.h
+++ b/include/fluent-bit/flb_output.h
@@ -20,7 +20,8 @@
 #ifndef FLB_OUTPUT_H
 #define FLB_OUTPUT_H
 
-#ifndef _XOPEN_SOURCE
+/* QNX rejects a valueless _XOPEN_SOURCE and needs none */
+#if !defined(_XOPEN_SOURCE) && !defined(__QNXNTO__)
 #define _XOPEN_SOURCE
 #endif
 
